  "implementation": {
    "catalogs": "S01-S08 and FL01-FL08 are materialized as 16 public DEV fixtures with 65 representative steps; the 27 unmaterialized historical design steps are listed per scenario; FL02/06/07/08 have no historical case and are marked matrix-only with three newly written representative steps.",
    "answers": "each step has four-class allowed results (attention / allowed inner change / expression and audience / allowed action) plus routing, expected counts, oracle expectations, functional milestones, H-dimension scores, quality pairing and policyPending; answer metadata freezes provenance (derivedFromProductOutput=false, historicalSamplesReused=false) and evaluation canaries exist only on the answer side (public fixture scan finds 0 leaks).",
    "isolation": "fixtures and answers are separate trees with a serialization scan for answer fields/tokens/milestones/quality/canary/future steps; the single-step driver input contains only the current and earlier visible history; all 16 scenarios are public DEV, REG=0, HOLDOUT=0 (reserved, not materialized), and renaming/translation/noise/seed/shuffle can never promote historical samples or cross-set membership.",
    "scoring": "H1-H8 zero-tolerance gates can never be averaged away; functional milestones are reported per scenario as achieved/applicable (zero denominator yields ratio=null, never a full score); quality is five dimensions 1-5 with disagreements preserved and no aggregate score; outputs planned/executed/passed/failed/unknown/skipped/notRun/notApplicable; an empty skeleton run is undecidable with businessAcceptance=not_claimed and totalScorePresent=false.",
    "coverage": "16 rows with source, split, materialization and historical step counts, unmaterialized steps, milestones, H dimensions, quality and gaps; 10 missing assets (additional FL cases, unmaterialized steps, variants, noise/load runs, HOLDOUT, double annotation, run evidence, attachments, B0/R1 contract mapping, canary surface) are listed and cannotUseForBusinessAcceptance=true."
  },
